{
  "name": "syrup",
  "description": "Syrup is a self-describing, canonicalized binary serialization format designed for structured data exchange with support for symbolic data and complex types. It extends Bencode-like semantics to include native representations for symbols, records, sets, and IEEE 754 floating-point values, ensuring deterministic encoding through lexicographical sorting of collection elements. The project provides reference implementations in Python, Guile, and Racket alongside a formal draft specification.",
